Z||000000||BENGAL4||01-30-2001||10:21 PM||||I need pics and suggestions for some exhaust tips. They are finally in the finishing stages of my 3800 II S/C swap, and I was asked what tips I wanted.<P>Suggestions?<P><BR>Bill<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||01-30-2001||10:31 PM||||How did you handle the exhaust?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||01-30-2001||11:57 PM||||I was thinking about going aftermarket, but the look of the fastback tips is too good to spend 100 bucks on aftermarket ones.  I say clean up the stock tips and use them...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||SloPonti||01-31-2001||12:24 AM||||here you go!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/sloponti/fiero1.jpg"> <P>and do not even say they are to ricey!! you can order these tips through super x motorsports! they are megs 4.5 inch tips!||||reg||1
Z||000004||BroCar 87||01-31-2001||12:46 AM||||Don't flame me, but I have seen an exhaust tip that may be called a little ricey. BUT looks verry nice. They were twin tips like what we have on our fiero's already, but they were a little bigger and were angled up at the end at a 45* angle. They were very nice tips! I will search the internet for a pic real quick.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tips.jpg"> <BR>Here is a pic of the muffler (the ones ricers use)that has the angled tips built directly into the muffler. The tips come with a single in dual out (just like our stock tips). They are a little bigger than our stock tips, but not as big as the pic shows. I believe they are made by Pilot. AutoZone sells Pilot Motorsports products. If your interested, check em out!<P>REMEMBER, I just wanted to show you some tips... I am not IN LOVE with these tips, so if you think they are butt ugly, its all good!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Just throwin out an option for unique tips.<P>BroCar 87<P>[This message has been edited by BroCar 87 (edited 01-31-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by BroCar 87 (edited 01-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jim Keyton||01-31-2001||01:29 AM||||Megs make some very nice stainless dual outlet tips in 3 and 3 1/2 inch. They run around $80 - $90 each, but they are very nice. check <A HREF="http://www.banzaisports.com/megs/megshome.htm" TARGET=_blank>www.banzaisports.com/megs/megshome.htm</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||01-31-2001||02:19 AM||||Did they run a muffler on your 3.8? If not, you may want to look at Supertrapps, or Hooker makes some tunable tips.  My dad has Ansa resonator tips on his 3.8 coversion. In my opinion, it is WAY too loud. Sounds cool bopping around town, but on the freeway when you are pulling 2000 rpm at 70 mph, it actually gets tiring.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Sleeper||01-31-2001||02:19 AM||||i'd say forget about tips and just DUMP the exhaust right after the muffler.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phil||01-31-2001||07:39 AM||||Stimp<BR>The Supertrapps or the Hookers aren't much quieter than the Ansas. I'm still trying to get my sound level down. I did hear a SC3800 with dual cats and Ansa tips, nice and quiet. Found a pic mine when it was red (shudder)with the Hookers. The handy thing about the Hookers is that they are only 10" long.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hookers.jpg">  <P><p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 01-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||BENGAL4||01-31-2001||10:42 AM||||I guess I should have mentioned what the exhaust system has. It has a cat and resonators but no muffler. They did this because I have to pass emissions in Ohio. <P>Thanks,<P>Bill||||reg||10
